<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zell am Harmersbach</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zell am Harmersbach is a small town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-forest">Black Forest</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, near Gengenbach. Recognised as a free imperial city in the 14th century, it was one of the smallest imperial estates, with only a few hundred inhabitants, until it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden">Baden</a> in 1803. Its pottery works, founded in 1794, became known as Zeller Keramik.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zell-am-harmersbach.jpg" alt="Zell am Harmersbach" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Holger Uwe Schmitt · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:15.7.2019_Besuch_in_Zell_am_Harmersbach._03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
